          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On Wednesday, July 15, 2015, at 10:37 PM, a witness on a parking lot observed three very bright red lights forming a triangle and flying at low altitude. The object emerged from behind a forest, headed towards the witness's building, then made a 45-degree turn and disappeared from their field of vision. Only one testimony was collected. Given the elements gathered (see the investigation report), namely:\n\n- The identical red color to that of lanterns.\n- The number corresponding to a classic group release of lanterns.\n- The simultaneous movement of the lanterns, carried by the wind and creating an illusion of psychological shape (movement in the direction of the dominant wind).\n- Behavior identical to that of objects subject to no or low wind: moderate speed.\n- Absence of noise.\n- Short observation duration (10 to 15 seconds), compatible with the lifespan of lanterns.\n- Proximity of installations conducive to lantern releases, located in the direction of observation and not visible from the witness's position.\n\nThe GEIPAN classifies this case as \"B,\" indicating a probable observation of Thai lanterns.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "efb2fc56c0236bef81615cb6d8deb5ad668e0d59dc8e43d08afa0376aec677f2"
        }
